FOUNDERS LEDGER
Sunday, September 6, 2026 | Edition 88

Good morning. Four things this week.

1) ROUNDS WE NOTICED
- Marlow Bio (San Diego) raised an $80M Series B led by Cormorant Capital for its protein-design platform.
- Quorum Compliance (Chicago) closed a $14M Series A led by Granite Peak Ventures; the product automates state-by-state licensing filings.
- Tinsley Freight Tech (Kansas City) raised a $6M seed from Alder Lane Ventures for less-than-truckload rating software.
- Ordinal Labs (New York) announced an $18M Series A led by Palisade Growth for developer tooling.

2) TERM SHEET WATCH
Seed-fund pro rata is getting squeezed. In six of the 24 Series A term sheets we saw in the last month, the lead asked existing seed investors to waive or cap their pro rata so the round could close at the target ownership. Seed funds are pushing back, and in two cases the founders ended up mediating. If you are raising an A, ask your lead about this before the term sheet, not after; it is a much easier conversation when nobody has signed anything.

3) CHART OF THE WEEK
Median time from seed close to Series A close, US software companies: 26 months for companies that raised an A in the first half of 2026, up from 19 months in 2021. The distribution has a long right tail; the 75th percentile is now 34 months. Chart: https://foundersledger.com/charts/seed-to-a-2026

4) WORTH READING
"How to run a reference call on your lead investor," by a three-time founder, including the two questions that get honest answers from other founders in the portfolio. https://foundersledger.com/reads/reference-your-lead

Have a good Sunday.
Colette

